  "briefing": {
    "title": "CONVERGENCE",
    "story": [
      "The towers sing. The planet listens. But the Chorus is waking all the way now,",
      "and Aether Prime's own defensive instinct is kicking in \u2014 the old, automated",
      "systems that have slept for centuries are stirring in the deep places.",
      "",
      "SERA VANE: \"We're getting energy spikes across the continent. The Chorus is",
      "calling up the old defenses \u2014 automated installations that want to shut down",
      "anything moving. We have to take them offline, or the whole binding collapses.\"",
      "",
      "MARSHAL CORR: \"Then we move. We end this. No more sitting on the defensive.\""
    ],
    "objectives": [
      "Destroy the three defense installations (orbital cannons)",
      "Protect the convergence node (your task anchor \u2014 defend the radar)"
    ]
  },
  "debrief": {
    "win": [
      "The cannons fall silent. Aether Prime's ancient reflexes tire, then sleep.",
      "The Chorus settles, bound now not just by choice, but by the orchestrated harmony",
      "of tower, cannon, and binding. The planet rests. The work of healing can begin.",
      "",
      "VANE: \"We did it. Against every odd, every god, every enemy... we did it.\""
    ],
    "lose": [
      "The cannons fire endlessly. The convergence node collapses under the onslaught.",
      "The binding, fragmented, fails. Aether Prime wakes fully, and nothing remains."
    ]
  },
